<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=tanning">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Chemistry</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanning</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3500 BCE</span> · Also known as hide tanning</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tanning is the process of treating the skins and hides of animals to produce leather, permanently altering the protein structure of the skin so that it is more durable and less liable to decomposition. Vegetable oil tanned leather footwear about 5,500 years old has been found in the Areni-1 cave in Vayots Dzor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, and on the remains of Ötzi. Tanning was being carried out at Mehrgarh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> between 7000 and 3300 BCE, and about 2500 BCE the Sumerians began using leather on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> wheels. Chrome tanning, using chromium salts instead of natural tannins, was developed in the 1800s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tanning.jpg" alt="Tanning" width="330" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Donar Reiskoffer · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanned_leather.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 3500 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Areni-1 cave, Armenia</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Mehrgarh, Pakistan (7000-3300 BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Mehrgarh is said to have tanned between 7000 and 3300 BCE, a range too wide to date the start. Leather working tools about 400,000 years old at Hoxne, England, show leather working, not tanning.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=tanning">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
